<title>USA: CKS Group Q1 shr $0.13 before charge.</title>
<headline>CKS Group Q1 shr $0.13 before charge.</headline>
<dateline>CUPERTINO, Calif. 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>CKS GROUP, INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>		  Pro Forma Consolidated Statements of Income (1)</p>
<p>							Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							 Mar 2,    Feb. 29,</p>
<p>							   1997	  1996</p>
<p>							   (Unaudited)</p>
<p> Revenues					   $23,563     $13,873</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>  Direct salaries and related expenses	6,722	 4,305</p>
<p>  Other direct operating expenses	     8,951	 5,365</p>
<p>  General and administrative expenses	 5,344	 2,864</p>
<p>    Total operating expenses		   21,017	12,534</p>
<p> Operating income				   2,546	 1,339</p>
<p> Other income, net				    523	   338</p>
<p> Income before income taxes		     3,069	 1,677</p>
<p> Income taxes					 1,142	   639</p>
<p> Net income					   1,927	 1,038</p>
<p> Pro forma net income per share		  0.13	  0.08</p>
<p> Shares used in per share computation	14,946	13,831</p>
<p>NOTE: (1) The pro forma consolidated statements of income give effect to the pooling of interests business combination between the company and McKinney &amp; Silver. The statement excludes a $1.6 million nonrecurring charge for merger costs recorded by the company and includes a tax provision as if M&amp;S had been a taxable C Corporation for all periods.</p>
<p>Excluding the charge, Q1 fiscal 1997 earnings would have been $0.06 a share.</p>
